Subject: Preserve cached window geometry when Accessibility queries fail

AX position and size queries previously returned zero-filled geometry on failure.
Return a status separately and update existing frames only after all required AX
queries and value conversions succeed. Relative resize commands report a failed
query instead of resizing from zero coordinates.

Resize events still synchronize fullscreen state when geometry is unavailable.
A failed fullscreen query preserves the cached state. Geometry-dependent signals,
frame updates, and resize correction require a successful frame query.
Read fullscreen state before geometry debounce so a later event can recover from
a failed state query even when the frame has already been updated.

New windows use WindowServer bounds when their initial AX query fails. If both
queries fail, preserve the existing zero-initialized creation behavior so the
window remains observed instead of being dropped without a guaranteed retry.

Base: https://github.com/asmvik/yabai/commit/dd845723416f5fe92af49fad5ebab00369e07edd
Source: https://github.com/asmvik/yabai/blob/dd845723416f5fe92af49fad5ebab00369e07edd/src/window.c#L736
Applies after macos-27.patch.

